<problem>
<!-- <title>Pure&#x2D;time DiffEq &#x2D; quadratic &#x2D; nonzero initial time</title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="aaa" from="-10" to="10" exclude="0" numToSelect="4" withReplacement="true" />

<function name="f" variables="t" symbolic="true"><math simplify="numbersPreserveOrder">$aaa[1] *t^2+$aaa[2] *t+$aaa[3]</math></function>
<function name="intfeval" variables="t" symbolic="true"><math simplify="true">$aaa[1]/3 *t^3+$aaa[2] /2*t^2+$aaa[3]*t</math></function>


<selectFromSequence name="lb" from="-5" to="5" exclude="0" />

<select name="f_name">g h p q r y z</select>
<math name="dxdt">d$f_name/dt</math>
<math name="x_lb" referencesAreFunctionSymbols="$f_name">$f_name ($lb)</math>

<math name="finalans" simplify="true">$$intfeval(t)+$C_value </math>
<math name="intfeval_C">$$intfeval(t)+C </math>
<math name="x_t" referencesAreFunctionSymbols="$f_name">$f_name (t)</math>
<math name="intfeval_lb">$$intfeval($lb)</math>
<math name="C_value" simplify="true">$aaa[4] -$intfeval_lb </math>


</setup>


<p>
Solve the pure-time differential equation <m>$dxdt  = <math extend="$f.formula" /></m> with initial condition <m>$x_lb  = $aaa[4] </m>.
</p>

<p>
<m>$x_t =</m> 
<answer>
<award>$finalans </award>
<award credit="0" name="noConstant">$intfeval </award>
<award credit="0" name="withC">$intfeval_C</award>
</answer>
</p>

<feedback condition="$noConstant">The solution $x_t must match the initial condition <m>$x_0  = $aaa[4] </m>.</feedback>
<feedback condition="$withC">Since we have an initial condition <m>$x_0  = $aaa[4] </m>, don't add an arbitrary constant <m>C</m>.  Instead, find the value of the constant so that the solution $x_t matches the initial condition.</feedback>

<p>
Do not round your answer to a decimal.
</p>

<solution>
<p>
The solution can be found using the indefinite integral <m>\displaystyle \int $f \, dt </m> and the initial condition  <m>$x_lb  = $aaa[4] </m>.  To evaluate the integral, we first use the sum and constant product rules for integration: 
</p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle \int $f \, dt  = $aaa[1]  \int t^2\,dt + $aaa[2] \int t\,dt + \int $aaa[3]\,dt</m>
</p>
<p>
We then evaluate each of these integrals using the power rule for integration and add the arbitrary constant:
</p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle <math extend="$intfeval.formula" />+C</m>
</p>
<p>
Next, we substitute in the initial condition <m>$x_lb  = $aaa[4] </m> and solve for <m>C</m>:
</p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle $aaa[4]  = $intfeval_lb +C = <math simplify="true">$intfeval_lb+C</math></m>
</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle C = $C_value </m>
</p>
<p>
Finally, we have:
</p>

<p>
<m>\displaystyle $x_t  = $finalans </m>
</p>


</solution>


</problem>